{"causes": ["The fragmentation of Korea into three kingdoms created a rich tapestry of legends and histories that needed documentation.", "The rise of the Goryeo Dynasty prompted a revival of interest in Korea's historical narratives to legitimize its rule.", "The influence of Buddhism in Korea during the 13th century encouraged the compilation of texts that integrated spiritual and historical elements."], "effects": ["The "Samguk Yusa" became a foundational text for understanding the Three Kingdoms period and Korean history as a whole.", "It influenced subsequent historians and literary works, reinforcing the importance of myth and legend in the narrative of Korean history.", "The text played a crucial role in the development of Korean nationalism during the 20th century, especially under colonial rule."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "goryeo-dynasty", "sourceName": "Goryeo Dynasty", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "samguk-yusa", "targetName": "Samguk Yusa", "context": "The Goryeo Dynasty commissioned the compilation of the "Samguk Yusa" to affirm its historical legitimacy in the late 13th century."}, {"sourceSlug": "korean-nationalism", "sourceName": "Korean Nationalism", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "samguk-yusa", "targetName": "Samguk Yusa", "context": "The narratives in the "Samguk Yusa" have significantly influenced the development of Korean nationalism throughout historical struggles."}, {"sourceSlug": "goguryeo", "sourceName": "Goguryeo", "verb": "CONTAINS", "targetSlug": "samguk-yusa", "targetName": "Samguk Yusa", "context": "The history of Goguryeo is prominently featured within the "Samguk Yusa," detailing its legendary origins and notable figures."}, {"sourceSlug": "silla", "sourceName": "Silla", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "samguk-yusa", "targetName": "Samguk Yusa", "context": "The tales of Silla's interactions with Goguryeo and Baekje occur significantly within the "Samguk Yusa," illustrating the political landscape of ancient Korea."}, {"sourceSlug": "baekje", "sourceName": "Baekje", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "samguk-yusa", "targetName": "Samguk Yusa", "context": "The historical accounts of Baekje's rise and fall are documented during the compilation period of the "Samguk Yusa"."}], "places": [{"name": "Goryeo, Korea", "role": "Cultural center"}, {"name": "Goguryeo, Korea", "role": "Historical kingdom"}, {"name": "Silla, Korea", "role": "Historical kingdom"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Samguk Yusa", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "samguk-yusa"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q485538", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samguk_yusa"], "tags": ["literary work", "Epic Poetry & Mythology", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Samguk Yusa contributed to the historical record of the Classical period. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "The "Samguk Yusa" is pivotal in shaping the narrative of Korea's ancient history, influencing cultural identity and historical scholarship, particularly during the Goryeo Dynasty and later periods of struggle.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-17T01:11:09Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29546401797", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Collection of legends, folktales and historical accounts relating to goguryeo, baekje, silla and other ancient korean states, compiled by iryeon Created by Il-yeon.", "newValue": "The "Samguk Yusa," or "Memorabilia of the Three Kingdoms," is a vital historical text compiled in the late 13th century by the monk Iryeon, chronicling the lore, legends, and historical narratives of Korea's Three Kingdoms period, which lasted from approximately 57 BC to AD 668. This work is significant for its preservation of Korean cultural identity, particularly in the context of the Goryeo Dynasty, which sought to solidify its historical legitimacy through the documentation of its predecessors. By encapsulating the histories of Goguryeo, Baekje, and Silla, the "Samguk Yusa" not only records events but also reflects the socio-political dynamics and cultural practices of ancient Korea, making it a cornerstone of Korean historiography.

The text encompasses a wide range of stories, from the origins of the Three Kingdoms to the legendary figures such as King Dongmyeong of Goguryeo and the tales of heroic deeds and divine interventions. It is structured into chapters that include both historical accounts and mythical narratives, thereby blurring the lines between history and legend. The compilation of these accounts was significant during a time when Korea was consolidating its national identity, as it provided a narrative framework that would be referenced by later historians and scholars.

The legacy of the "Samguk Yusa" extends beyond its initial compilation; it has influenced subsequent historical writings and has been a source of inspiration in literature, art, and popular culture in Korea. It played a pivotal role in the revival of interest in Korea's ancient past during times of foreign domination, particularly during the Japanese occupation in the early 20th century. The text continues to be studied and revered, symbolizing the resilience of Korean culture and identity through centuries of change."}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-17T01:11:09Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29546401797", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Cultural, artistic, or intellectual creation"], "newValue": ["The fragmentation of Korea into three kingdoms created a rich tapestry of legends and histories that needed documentation.", "The rise of the Goryeo Dynasty prompted a revival of interest in Korea's historical narratives to legitimize its rule.", "The influence of Buddhism in Korea during the 13th century encouraged the compilation of texts that integrated spiritual and historical elements."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-17T01:11:09Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29546401797", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission"], "newValue": ["The "Samguk Yusa" became a foundational text for understanding the Three Kingdoms period and Korean history as a whole.", "It influenced subsequent historians and literary works, reinforcing the importance of myth and legend in the narrative of Korean history.", "The text played a crucial role in the development of Korean nationalism during the 20th century, especially under colonial rule."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-17T01:11:09Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29546401797", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "samguk-yusa", "sourceName": "Samguk Yusa", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "era-classical", "targetName": "Classical